From: Noxwell <beebono@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: qcom-spmi-adc5: add BAT_THERM_100K_PU channel

PMI632 routes the battery thermistor to ADC5_BAT_THERM_100K_PU (0x4a),
which is missing from the channel table, so a device tree referencing
it fails to probe.
---
diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5.c b/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5.c
index 83ecd3a..426ca11 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5.c
@@ -544,6 +544,8 @@ static const struct adc5_channels adc5_chans_pmic[ADC5_MAX_CHANNEL] = {
 					SCALE_HW_CALIB_XOTHERM)
 	[ADC5_BAT_ID_100K_PU]	= ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("bat_id", 0,
 					SCALE_HW_CALIB_DEFAULT)
+	[ADC5_BAT_THERM_100K_PU] = ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("bat_therm_100k_pu", 0,
+					SCALE_HW_CALIB_THERM_100K_PULLUP)
 	[ADC5_AMUX_THM1_100K_PU] = ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("amux_thm1_100k_pu", 0,
 					SCALE_HW_CALIB_THERM_100K_PULLUP)
 	[ADC5_AMUX_THM2_100K_PU] = ADC5_CHAN_TEMP("amux_thm2_100k_pu", 0,
